# VS Code: commit the curated shared project config, ignore everything else
# (extensions auto-write machine-specific files into .vscode/). The broad ignore
# MUST come before the `!` whitelist — later rules win in .gitignore. `!/.vscode/`
# re-includes the DIRECTORY first: a global excludesFile with a bare `.vscode/`
# is common, and git never descends into an ignored directory, so without it the
# file-level whitelist below silently does nothing for those users. Anchored with
# a leading slash so it only re-includes the ROOT .vscode/ — an unanchored
# `!.vscode/` would also un-ignore nested ones (e.g. packages/foo/.vscode/ in a
# monorepo) whose machine-specific files the root-anchored `.vscode/*` above
# does not cover.
.vscode/*
!/.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json

